Done. Type check and tests pass (7/7, including the 3 new ones).
Fixed. The bug was at src/sim.ts:43 — the growth check was `if (foodSurplus >= 0)`, so a break-even turn (production exactly equals consumption, surplus = 0) still counted as a surplus and bumped population by 1. That's why settlements barely making ends meet kept growing every turn.

Change: `>= 0` → `> 0`, matching the documented behavior ("grows by 1 if there was a food surplus this turn").

I also added a regression test block for `advanceTurn` in tests/sim.test.ts covering three cases:
- break-even (10 produced / 10 consumed) → population stays put
- surplus (10 / 8) → population grows by 1, food bank grows by the surplus
- deficit (5 / 10) → population stays put

Verification: `npm run typecheck` passes and `npm run test` passes — 7/7 tests, including the 3 new ones.


